WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.717
Open Chat from the Omni IC menu to find the
conversations available to your account.

00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:11.167
Read the channel name before opening it so that you
can choose the right audience for the update.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:13.940
Open the Academy readiness training channel.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.341
The conversation heading tells you where your update
would go.

00:00:17.521 --> 00:00:24.668
A search team could use a channel like this for
staging coordination, and a security team could use
one for a shift handoff.

00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:28.081
Use the message box to draft a concise update.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.693
This exercise keeps the update unsent.

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:37.124
For a real handoff, check the channel and the
information your department allows you to share
before sending.

00:00:37.444 --> 00:00:40.132
Open Notifications to check the inbox.

00:00:40.312 --> 00:00:43.235
This browser says the inbox is unavailable here.

00:00:43.415 --> 00:00:50.199
If you see this state, check which device and
notification channel your department expects you to
use for alerts.

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:55.447
Under Push Notifications in Settings, use Test alert
sounds to preview a tone.

00:00:55.627 --> 00:00:58.656
Message and Notification have separate controls.

00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:01.289
This is a sound test on the current device.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:06.431
In the Audio section, check Microphone and Speaker to
see the selected devices.

00:01:06.611 --> 00:01:14.312
Test the audio at the desk before an industrial drill
or a community standby so the operator knows which
equipment is in use.
